---Contains the OpenID Connect (OIDC) configuration information for Single Sign-On (SSO) authentication, including identity provider settings and client credentials.
---@class aws.wickr.OidcConfigInfo
---@field applicationName? aws.wickr.GenericString The name of the OIDC application as registered with the identity provider.
---@field clientId? aws.wickr.GenericString The OAuth client ID assigned by the identity provider for authentication requests.
---@field companyId aws.wickr.GenericString Custom identifier your end users will use to sign in with SSO.
---@field scopes aws.wickr.GenericString The OAuth scopes requested from the identity provider, which determine what user information is accessible (e.g., 'openid profile email').
---@field issuer aws.wickr.GenericString The issuer URL of the identity provider, which serves as the base URL for OIDC endpoints and configuration discovery.
---@field clientSecret? distilled.Secret The OAuth client secret used to authenticate the application with the identity provider.
---@field secret? distilled.Secret An additional secret credential used by the identity provider for authentication.
---@field redirectUrl? aws.wickr.GenericString The callback URL where the identity provider redirects users after successful authentication. This URL must be registered with the identity provider.
---@field userId? aws.wickr.GenericString The claim field from the OIDC token to use as the unique user identifier (e.g., 'email', 'sub', or a custom claim).
---@field customUsername? aws.wickr.GenericString A custom field mapping to extract the username from the OIDC token when the standard username claim is insufficient.
---@field caCertificate? aws.wickr.GenericString The X.509 CA certificate for validating SSL/TLS connections to the identity provider when using self-signed or enterprise certificates.
---@field applicationId? number The unique identifier for the registered OIDC application. Valid range is 1-10.
---@field ssoTokenBufferMinutes? number The grace period in minutes before the SSO token expires when the system should proactively refresh the token to maintain seamless user access.
---@field extraAuthParams? aws.wickr.GenericString Additional authentication parameters to include in the OIDC authorization request as a query string. Useful for provider-specific extensions.

---Contains OAuth token information returned from the identity provider, including access tokens, ID tokens, and PKCE parameters used for secure authentication.
---@class aws.wickr.OidcTokenInfo
---@field codeVerifier? aws.wickr.GenericString The PKCE (Proof Key for Code Exchange) code verifier, a cryptographically random string used to enhance security in the OAuth flow.
---@field codeChallenge? aws.wickr.GenericString The PKCE code challenge, a transformed version of the code verifier sent during the authorization request for verification.
---@field accessToken? aws.wickr.GenericString The OAuth access token that can be used to access protected resources on behalf of the authenticated user.
---@field idToken? aws.wickr.GenericString The OpenID Connect ID token containing user identity information and authentication context as a signed JWT.
---@field refreshToken? aws.wickr.GenericString The OAuth refresh token that can be used to obtain new access tokens without requiring the user to re-authenticate.
---@field tokenType? aws.wickr.GenericString The type of access token issued, typically 'Bearer', which indicates how the token should be used in API requests.
---@field expiresIn? number The lifetime of the access token in seconds, indicating when the token will expire and need to be refreshed.

